{"name":"Beryllonite","hex":"#e9e5d7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beryllonite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rare mineral, sodium beryllium phosphate, with the chemical formula NaBePO4; found especially in Maine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beryllonite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beryllonite","blocks":[{"text":"Beryllonite is a rare phosphate mineral with formula NaBePO4. The tabular to prismatic monoclinic crystals vary from colorless to white or pale yellowish, and are transparent with a vitreous luster. Twinning is common and occurs in several forms. It exhibits perfect cleavage in one direction. The hardness is 5.5 to 6 and the specific gravity is 2.8. Refractive indices are nα = 1.552, nβ = 1.558 and nγ = 1.561. A few crystals have been cut and faceted, but, as the refractive index is no higher than that of quartz, they do not make very brilliant gemstones."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Beryllonite.jpg/330px-Beryllonite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beryllonite","wikidata":"Q2040729"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Strawberry on white background","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Strawberry_on_white_background.jpg/500px-Strawberry_on_white_background.jpg","ratio":1.618,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Strawberry_on_white_background.jpg","share":0.671875},{"title":"The American journal of science (1889) (18151924781)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/The_American_journal_of_science_%281889%29_%2818151924781%29.jpg/500px-The_American_journal_of_science_%281889%29_%2818151924781%29.jpg","ratio":0.536510376633359,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_American_journal_of_science_(1889)_(18151924781).jpg","share":0.576875},{"title":"Piece of chocolate cake on a white plate decor